{"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item"]]},"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/isDoor","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"isDoor"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"kind":"text","text":" { "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"get"},{"kind":"text","text":" }"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"mentions","mentions":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ContainersDoorsAndLocks"]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Either the map says so, by hanging a way through on the thing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"code":"hall.north(garden, via: frontDoor)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), or the item declares "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/door","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The first covers every door a player can walk through, which is why most"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"games never declare the second."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It answers the same for every room, which is deliberate. A rule that"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"wants “a door ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"here","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":"” — the one the player could walk through from where","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"they stand — wants the room’s exits, not this. What this is for is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"question a verb asks about the thing in front of it: knocking on a door"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"is a different act from knocking on a bench, wherever either is standing."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Gnusto"}],"title":"isDoor","symbolKind":"property","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"isDoor","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Property","role":"symbol","externalID":"s:6Gnusto4ItemV6isDoorSbvp"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/gnusto\/item\/isdoor"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"True if this item is a door — the front door, the trap door, the grating."}],"references":{"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Item":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Item","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A thing in the world.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"Item","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/item","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Item","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/door":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/door","title":"door","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/door","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"door","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ItemTrait","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto9ItemTraitV"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The item is a door — something a verb may reasonably treat as a way through","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rather than as a thing.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Item/isDoor":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/item\/isdoor","title":"isDoor","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/isDoor","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"isDoor"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"}],"abstract":[{"text":"True if this item is a door — the front door, the trap door, the grating.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto":{"abstract":[{"text":"An engine for writing interactive fiction in Swift.","type":"text"}],"title":"Gnusto","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto","role":"collection"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/ContainersDoorsAndLocks":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/containersdoorsandlocks","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ContainersDoorsAndLocks","title":"Containers, Doors, and Locks","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Hold things, open and close, lock with keys, and gate the map.","type":"text"}],"role":"article"}}}